<!-- One document, and every address it is worth indexing at. About and Contact
     are views of index.html reached by ?p=, so these are query URLs rather than
     paths; the page sets a matching rel=canonical per route, without which the
     root's canonical would tell a crawler both of them are duplicates of it.

     THE GUIDE PAGES ARE FILES, not views, so they are listed by path — and
     listed ONCE. They are English-only copies of two MeshCore documents, so
     they make no hreflang claim and have no ?lang=nb address, the same way Home
     does not for the opposite reason.

     BOTH ARE HERE, THOUGH ONLY ONE IS IN THE BAR. The bar carries a single
     "Regions guide" item and the rail on those pages links the pair, so the
     technical reference is one click further in but is a full page with its own
     address and its own canonical. The `seo` group knows this: it builds the
     expected list from the bar's links AND the rail's, which is why adding a
     third document to build.py's DOCS fails here until it is listed.

     THE LANGUAGE IS PART OF THE ADDRESS, but only where the translation is real.
     About in Norwegian is a Norwegian document and is listed; the page declares
     rel=alternate hreflang between the pair. Home is NOT listed twice — it is an
     English tool with Norwegian help text around English labels, a map and a CLI
     block, so ?lang=nb there canonicals back to the root as the duplicate it is.

     No <lastmod>: nothing here would keep it honest, and a stale date is worse
     than none. The `seo` test group asserts this list against the links in the
     bar and the languages the page offers, so neither a fourth page nor a third
     language can be added without appearing here. -->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/?p=contact</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/?p=about</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/regions-guide.html</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/regions-reference.html</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/?p=contact&amp;lang=nb</loc></url>
  <url><loc>https://meshno.github.io/?p=about&amp;lang=nb</loc></url>
</urlset>
